What's new in version 0.2.10

* The graph fills the screen again, and clicks and drags reach every column of it: where the terminfo only knows X10
  mouse reports (Amazon Linux), hmon asks the terminal for SGR reports and reads them itself, instead of 0.2.9's
  narrower graph

What's new in version 0.2.9

* Graph clicks and drags land on the bar under the pointer in wide terminals too: where mouse reports are the old X10
  kind, which can't say a column past 223, the graph now stays within those columns instead of running out of reach

What's new in version 0.2.8

* Installer: no "hmon: command not found" at the end of an update where sudo leaves /usr/local/bin off its PATH
  (Amazon Linux); it now also reports "Updated old -> new" there
* hmon configure asks for sudo itself, like hmon update and hmon uninstall, so no command needs "sudo hmon"
* 0.2.7 was tagged but never published (a test failed on Python 3.7's curses); its changes, below, come with 0.2.8

What's new in version 0.2.7

* At 10 s and 1 min bars the live column shows what runs now, as htop does: a container stopped a moment ago is gone
  at once, instead of lasting until its bar ends; longer bars keep their statistic, so today's peak stays findable
* hmon uninstall removes hmon, and asks separately whether the recorded samples and the settings go too
* A range of bars side by side: Space at one bar and Left / Right, or a drag across the graph, and the table shows
  each bar as a column (RES, or CPU% on the CPU graph; '-' where a process wasn't running); Esc goes back to one bar
* The mouse wheel scrolls down too where ncurses has its old mouse interface (no button 5), as on Amazon Linux 2
* "New update available" stands out: black on yellow, set off from the key bar
* hmon update says what it's doing before each step that waits on the network
* Setup: the time zone list shows each zone's abbreviation, and typing matches it or the offset too (ist, +05:30)

What's new in version 0.2.6

* Shift+Tab cycles the graph tabs backwards

What's new in version 0.2.5

* hmon update installs the newest release (asking for sudo), keeping the interval and retention already set
* The viewer says "New update available" at the bottom right when a newer release is out; it asks GitHub once at
  start, in the background, and stays quiet without network
* Key bars: a space between each key and what it does, and two between items (F1 Help  F2 Setup); keys that don't
  fit whole are left off instead of cut

What's new in version 0.2.4

* Dragging keeps up with the mouse: while the button is held only the highlight is repainted, not the whole screen,
  so the selection follows the pointer and the copy happens as soon as you let go
* Key pairs read apart in the function bar and help: [ / ] and ← / → instead of [] and ←→

What's new in version 0.2.3

* Dragging selects text: what you drag over is highlighted and copied to the clipboard when you let go (OSC 52), and
  no longer clicks what's under the release
* Go to: Esc or a click cancels; Backspace and Ctrl+U edit what's typed
* Ctrl+C quits quietly, with status 130, instead of printing a traceback

What's new in version 0.2.2

* Installer: an update keeps the sampling interval and retention already set instead of asking again
* Installer: prints each step, and no longer waits on journald where the journal is kept in memory (Storage=volatile);
  the journal flush, tmpfiles and service restart have time limits, the download retries
* Setup: a Mouse setting (on/off, saved) for selecting text by dragging; with it on, Shift+drag still selects

What's new in version 0.2.1

* Clicks act on release, as in htop, so Help, Setup and the sort panel no longer close when the button is let go
* Setup opens a dropdown for every setting (type to filter); time zones come from the system's zone database
* Setup's Recording section, and `hmon configure`, change the sampling interval and retention the installer asked
* `+` always unfolds and `-` always folds; Enter still toggles
* Function bar: a space after full-width labels (F3Search F4Filter)

What's new in version 0.2.0

* Look and keys of htop: meters, colors, column titles with the sort arrow, function bar, F1 help, F3 search,
  F4 filter, F5 tree/list, F6 sort, M/P/N/I, mouse
* Processes grouped into apps (systemd units, containers under docker, programs at the top of a process tree),
  folded by default, with htop's process tree inside
* Live: the newest column samples /proc every 1.5 s, and recorded samples are picked up as they land
* Graph of memory, CPU, load or swap at 10 s to 1 day per column, with Average, Maximum, Minimum, p50, p90, p99
* F2 Setup for the time zone and defaults, saved to ~/.config/hmon/hmonrc
* Go to everyday dates and zones: 12/10/2026 14:30 IST, 2 Feb 2025 UTC
* hmon export (a .tar.gz dump or SQLite), hmon FILE.tar.gz, hmon sql "SELECT ..."
* Installer asks how often to sample and how long to keep it, with the disk that takes
* No sudo needed to view, except where /proc hides other users' processes
* Records each process's parent and cgroup, load 5/15 and swap total; files from 0.1.0 still load

What's new in version 0.1.0

* First release: per-minute host, container and process samples, a time-graph viewer, `hmon at`
